---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/sequenzy-vs-yotpo-email-sms';
const title = "Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email & SMS: migration considerations";
const desc = "Yotpo announced Email & SMS deprecation; evaluate a replacement while preserving review and loyalty dependencies.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I choose Yotpo Email & SMS as a new 2026 platform?",
    "answer": "Yotpo announced full deprecation for December 31, 2025. Treat this as replacement planning and confirm any remaining account access with Yotpo."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does changing email require moving Yotpo Reviews?",
    "answer": "The email migration notice alone does not establish that. Inventory review and loyalty dependencies separately and verify supported connections."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
<a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
<header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sequenzy vs Yotpo Email &amp; SMS: migration considerations</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">Yotpo announced Email & SMS deprecation; evaluate a replacement while preserving review and loyalty dependencies.</p></header>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
<h2>This is a migration decision in 2026</h2>
<p>Yotpo announced full deprecation of its Email and SMS products for December 31, 2025. Its notice recommends Attentive and Omnisend as migration partners. This page therefore does not recommend buying Yotpo Email & SMS as a current alternative. Sequenzy may enter a replacement shortlist, but the announcement is not an endorsement of Sequenzy or evidence that it reproduces historical Yotpo workflows.</p>
<h2>Separate messaging from reviews and loyalty</h2>
<p>The Email & SMS announcement does not mean all Yotpo products share that status. Inventory review collection, storefront review display, loyalty benefits, email and SMS as separate dependencies. For a proposed beauty-store migration, mark every message that contains review content, points or tier benefits. Confirm which service owns each data field and whether the replacement has a documented supported integration. A Shopify customer tag should not be assumed to carry live point balances or product reviews.</p>
<h2>Recover records before promising continuity</h2>
<p>Check what exports and account access remain available with Yotpo support; do not assume a historical account can still send or export today. Seek contact identifiers, channel permissions, suppression records, workflow definitions and creative assets. Record any missing timestamps or fields explicitly. Keep email and SMS permission separate and carry exclusions into the replacement. Existing review data and marketing permission are different records with different uses.</p>
<h2>Validate the data dependency before the design</h2>
<p>A proposed loyalty-member winback needs reliable tier and benefit data. Check field meaning, freshness, missing-value handling and eligibility for an offer. Use internal cases for a newly upgraded member, a refunded order and an unknown tier. If the replacement cannot obtain the data, simplify the message or retain a supported specialist connection. Do not replace live point balances with stale text merely to make the template look complete.</p>
<h2>Scope Sequenzy as a candidate</h2>
<p>Sequenzy advertises Shopify customer/order sync and volume-based email pricing. Its paid SMS/MMS product is marked Beta, so confirm destination coverage, sender setup and account availability before including SMS in the replacement plan. Review and loyalty connections need separate verification. Compare the candidate against the migration partners Yotpo names on the actual required fields and channels; no winner is established by the old suite-versus-strategy framing.</p>
<h2>Rebuild the post-purchase calendar</h2>
<p>List order confirmation, education, review request, loyalty notification and promotional follow-up with their owners and stop conditions. Rehearse internal orders before launch. Keep review requests with the appropriate review service where that configuration remains supported, and avoid adding a second request from the new sender. For refunds, cancellations and reordered products, check which scheduled messages should stop. A new platform does not automatically coordinate other services.</p>
<h2>Budget for replacement rather than imaginary bundle savings</h2>
<p>Retain actual continuing Reviews or Loyalty charges in both sides of the estimate. Add the replacement email workload, destination-specific text costs, sender migration and field-mapping labor. Do not compare an invented historical suite invoice with an email-only quote. Sign off when required records and message owners are accounted for, unresolved fields have a workable fallback, and the replacement has passed the store-specific tests. Historical revenue percentages on this page have been removed because no underlying tests were available.</p>
<h2>Sources and scope</h2>
<p>Checked November 25, 2026. Vendor documentation establishes advertised scope, not tested account behavior. Exercises above are proposed, not completed merchant tests.</p>
<ul>
<li><a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo deprecation and migration notice</a></li>
<li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">Sequenzy feature and channel scope</a></li>
<li><a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/sequenzy">Sequenzy Shopify listing</a></li>
</ul>
</article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
